    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the boost pump inlet installation, showing the filter housing in both element lengths, the downstream regulator and the distribution hardware inside the tank.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the boost pump inlet installation inside the wing tank, from the pump inlet face outward to the filter housing and the regulator.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left inner pump position; the other three positions use the same breakdown. Items 10 and 10A are the two housing standards and they are not interchangeable, because the taller housing is required to take the longer element. Order the housing and the element together. The nut at item 30 is common to both standards."
    },
